Package: svyexpo
Title: Link Survey Clusters to Raster Exposures and Fit Bayesian Spatial Models
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R:
    person("Patrick", "Attey-Yeboah", , "your.email@example.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Tools for exposure-outcome analysis of geocoded household
    surveys such as the Demographic and Health Surveys (DHS) and Multiple
    Indicator Cluster Surveys (MICS). The package standardises survey
    records to a common schema, assigns clusters to administrative areas
    from the Database of Global Administrative Areas (GADM), extracts raster
    exposures within displacement-aware buffers without loading full rasters
    into memory, builds spatial adjacency structures, and fits BYM2 models
    with optional spatially varying coefficients using INLA.
